---
name: smoke-report-smoke
version: 1.0.0
description: Smoke report markdown rendered from the canonical smoke JSON.
format: markdown
required_variables:
  - report.status
  - report.timestamp
  - report.binary_sha
  - report.duration_secs
  - report.summary.pass
  - report.summary.fail
  - report.summary.skip
  - report.rows
---
# Smoke

- status: `{{ report.status }}`
- timestamp: `{{ report.timestamp }}`
- binary SHA: `{{ report.binary_sha }}`
- duration secs: `{{ report.duration_secs }}`
- summary: `pass={{ report.summary.pass }}`, `fail={{ report.summary.fail }}`, `skip={{ report.summary.skip }}`
- row semantics: `PASS` means every command in the row exited `0`; `FAIL`
  records the first failing command only and does not claim sibling commands in
  that row were executed after the failure

| Row | Flow | Verdict | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
{% for row in report.rows -%}
| `{{ row.id }}` | {{ row.flow }} | `{{ row.verdict }}` | {{ row.notes }} |
{% endfor %}

{% set deviations = report.rows | selectattr("verdict", "ne", "PASS") | list -%}
{% if deviations %}

## Deviations

{% for row in deviations -%}
### `{{ row.id }}`

- observed: {{ row.get("observed_behavior", "n/a") }}
- expected: {{ row.get("expected_behavior", "n/a") }}
- likely root cause: {{ row.get("likely_root_cause", "n/a") }}
- artifact: {{ row.get("artifact_pointer", "n/a") }}

{% endfor -%}
{% endif %}
